      "content": "To frame this academically, acknowledge that the confidence interval defines the precision of your estimate, noting that while the result is statistically reliable, the effect size could vary significantly depending on the underlying sample variability. You can describe this \"noise\" not as a flaw but as a constraint of observational data, carving out a specific paragraph that discusses how a wider interval suggests we need even more granular data to pinpoint exactly how green space influences social bonds. This approach demonstrates rigor by accepting statistical limitations as inherent to social science research rather than casting doubt on your entire study's validity. Finally, position this finding as a starting point for future longitudinal studies to narrow that interval and strengthen causal claims.",
