      "content": "thanks for the advice. one more thing—i was reading a paper that mentioned \"sampling error\" or \"unexplained variance\" can sometimes feel like these \"hidden forces\" that mess up the data patterns. is there a formal way to talk about those unexpected outliers or the stuff that doesn't fit the model without sounding like i'm just making excuses for bad data? i want to stay professional but i'm struggling to find the right words for that \"unpredictable\" element in the results.",
